 "notes": "Two-copy census: among the 360 two-qutrit stabilizer states, the three-term decompositions of |N>^2 span 13 distinct three-spaces, three of which contain four stabilizer rays rather than three, and the plane through |N> itself contains four rays. The sparsest representation of |N>^5 as a combination of products (ray of such a space) x (ray of the same space) x (ray of the plane) has exactly 10 terms on each of the three four-ray spaces (HiGHS, optimal; 64 words per cell), against 12 by tensoring 4 x 3. The ten terms are products of two two-qutrit and one one-qutrit stabilizer state; the coefficients were solved exactly over Q(omega_3) after factoring the term normalizations sqrt(3^k) and 36 sqrt 6 out, and are of the forms (+-sqrt 6 +- 3 sqrt 2 I)/16 and (-sqrt 2 - sqrt 6 I)/16. Implied exponent log_3(10)/5 = 0.4192, below log_3(4)/3 = 0.4206 from chi(N^3) <= 4. Barren routes recorded: the record span at three copies is a basis dictionary (3+3 words give exactly 16); the same construction gives nothing for H3 (exactly 8 words at four copies over every four-ray span), T3 (its two-copy decomposition is unique with a basis span), or S (no span with extra rays through S, S^2, or the three-copy record). Word ranks at six copies capped at 15 were undecided after 900 s locally and are running longer elsewhere."
